{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Jacob gave Esau bread and lentil stew.</b> Here Scripture reveals what it mentioned above, ״ויזד יעקב נזיד״ — that it was a stew of lentils. And it would have been more proper to explain this above and say ״ויזד יעקב נזיד עדשים״, and afterward say ״ויעקב נתן לעשו לחם ונזיד״. But it is possible to say that Scripture intended to indicate Esau's arrogance and pride, and his lowliness; and because of this it did not wish to mention before the sale what kind of stew it was — for the listener would suppose it was an important and distinguished dish, since he sold his birthright for it. Therefore Scripture delayed mentioning the name of the stew until after the sale, as one who says: the birthright that he sold for the stew mentioned above — it was nothing but a lentil stew. And this is a sign of the disposition of his evil soul, that he despised the birthright."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:13.284891230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}